  "chapter": {
    "number": 38,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(39) For the end, a Song of David, to Idithun."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I set a guard on my mouth, while the sinner stood in my presence.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I was dumb, and humbled myself, and kept silence from good words; and my grief was renewed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My heart grew hot within me, and a fire would kindle in my meditation: I spoke with my tongue,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, make me to know my end, and the number of my days, what it is; that I may know what I lack.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold, you have made my days",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 73
          },
          {
            "text": "old; and my existence is as nothing before you: nay, every man living is altogether vanity. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Surely man walks in a",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 74
          },
          {
            "text": "shadow; nay, he is disquieted in vain: he lays up treasures, and knows not for whom he shall gather them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And now what is my expectation? is it not the Lord? and my ground of hope is with you. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me from all my transgressions: you have made me a reproach to the foolish.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I was",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 75
          },
          {
            "text": "dumb, and opened not my mouth; for you are he that made me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remove your scourges from me: I have fainted by reason of the strength of your hand.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You chasten man with rebukes for iniquity, and you make his life to consume away like a spider's web; nay, every man is disquieted in vain. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, listen to my prayer and my supplication: attend to my tears: be not silent, for I am a sojourner in the land, and a stranger, as all my fathers were.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Spare me, that I may be refreshed, before I depart, and be no more.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 73,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Alex. a span long.",
